{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/fake_host/replay.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:48:43.589971Z","id":"1f022790de8e3559069196d8848b580ecea6d4d7a95677d8578275fc7ef54d64","body":{"detail":"MemoryHub::serve (crates/clax-testkit/src/fake_host/memory.rs:166-172) answers a serve that has nothing to send as the hub answers it when its wait is over and moves the HostClock there; HttpTransport just sends the request. The fixture's serve at at_ms 8200 has wait_ms 12000 and held_ms 12000: against a daemon on a manual clock that request blocks until the clock is advanced, so a routes test that replays the fixture over HttpTransport needs a ScriptWorld or transport wrapper that advances the clock while the request is in flight. replay() does not check held_ms itself (the hub's own test, crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces/tests.rs Replay::serve, does).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":142},"end":{"line":189},"content_hash":"fc04426201afea889c43da25ac9ceb48f090aa267049e4d7ac5cbc4933c5583f"},"summary":"replay() leaves a serve step's held_ms to the transport: a replay against a real server must move the daemon's clock while that serve is held","tags":["routes","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/fake_host/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:48:43.590074Z","id":"7b78c8064b2cf14f466721a249b9156b6db95ac7e46cc7c496afa5b508e83d92","body":{"detail":"Behaviour::Accept with When::Rounds(0) sends {id, accepted: true} and {id, result} in one ServeRequest. Hub::open (crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces.rs:1306-1310) ignores a second answer for an ID within one serve, so the result is dropped and the call ends unknown_outcome. Once the hub takes accepted and a later result for one ID in the same serve, this test can use When::Rounds(0) and expect serve_until(...) == Ok(2).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":282},"end":{"line":282},"content_hash":"9a9b3851c403e314b1c63e52264f2f848cc506c620d3f3476f7c6d02333d40ac"},"summary":"The resume test answers accepted and the result in two rounds (When::Rounds(1)) because the hub takes only the first answer per ID in one serve","tags":["revisit:Hub::open takes accepted then a result for one ID in one serve","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/fake_host/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T20:10:14.221325Z","id":"8bdeafe0f7ac73b9ae4f34cedf67770c4d5130abd86323bc851fc88e480a0259","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7b78c8064b2cf14f466721a249b9156b6db95ac7e46cc7c496afa5b508e83d92","summary":"Hub::open now takes accepted and a later result for one ID in one serve: a_dropped_connection_skips_rounds_and_its_host_resumes_its_registration uses When::Rounds(0) and expects serve_until(...) == Ok(2), and passes (//crates/clax-testkit:clax_testkit_lib_test, 22 passed). The record can be closed as fixed.","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
